-- title:
--   Layered node charts and Hasse germs at a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathtt{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. The field $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (coefficientwise, inside Laurent series) of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H=\mathtt{levelH}\ q\ M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ is the analogous base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathbb Q(\,j(\mathsf q^{d}):d\mid M'\,)$, and $\mathrm{hle}$ asserts $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$.
--
--   Data over the residue field: $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'=\kappa(j(\mathsf q),j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$ over $\kappa$, and $\mathrm{hW}$ says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. those $w$ which are rational over $\kappa$, are affine geometric places, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-generator in the supersingular $j$-set $\mathtt{ssJSet}\ q\ \kappa$; $s\in W$ is one such place. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'$ with kernel the maximal ideal, cutting out $A$ on constants and inducing $A\to\kappa$ there, together with a place map preserving degrees, the scaling property that every nonzero $f$ has a constant multiple in the integers with nonzero residue, and compatibility of divisors with the place map. The hypothesis $\mathrm{hR}_0$ says that for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Constants: $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$; the hypotheses $\mathrm{hdvr}$, $\mathrm{hunif}$, $\mathrm{hhens}$, $\mathrm{hres}$ state that $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; $\mathrm{h}\kappa$ states that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $A\cap k_0$.
--
--   Auxiliary arithmetic data: $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ with $u$ a unit of $A$. A layer family is given: a type $\iota$, finite extensions $K_n$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cut out by $A$, a least index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$, and cofinality $\mathrm{hKcof}$: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in the image of some $K_n$. Moreover $\pi_t\in A$ satisfies $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q$, and $\mathrm{htame}$ states that every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ whose tame character $A.\mathrm{tameCharacter}\ \pi_t$ is $1$ fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. Finally $K_b$ is the bottom intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (so $K_b=k_0$), $A_b$ is the valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, and $\varpi_b\neq0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   With $k_0$ acting on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ satisfying four conditions (the level-field conditions): $F_0$ consists exactly of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$; $F_0$ together with the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generates everything, $k_0(\overline{\mathbb Q})\sqcup F_0=\top$; $F_0$ is stable under $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ for every $\zeta$ in $\mathtt{Idx}\ q$ (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is linearly disjoint from $F_0$ over $k_0$ in the form: for $K'/k_0$ finite, any family $c_i\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and any $a_i\in k_0(K')\sqcup F_0$ with $\sum_i c_ia_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   The statement then quantifies over a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$; a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure; witnesses that the image of $j_q$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a witness $\mathrm{hJK}$ that $J:=\mathtt{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q$, the series $j$ with $\mathsf q$ replaced by $\mathsf q^{q}$, lies in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$; a Hasse lift $a_0\in k_0\cap A$ with $\overline{a_0}^{\,q}=s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j_q$; and a finite set $\mathtt{nodes}$ of subrings of $F_0$. These are subject to one large hypothesis block, whose groups are the following (inner clauses summarised where indicated).
--
--   (W1) $W_0$ cuts out $A$ on $k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, and its maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$. (W2) $W_0$ is centred at $s$: for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$ whose base change lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and which is regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j_q$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of $g$ and $c$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$. (W3) $W_0$ is invariant under the level automorphisms: for $\zeta$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $f\in F_0$ with $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f\in F_0$, membership of $f$ in $W_0$ is equivalent to that of its image.
--
--   (B) The chart clauses for $B$: the $A_b$-algebra structure is the one induced by $A_b\subseteq K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $B$ is contained in $k_0(K_b)\sqcup F_0$ and this field is the fraction field of $B$ (every element is $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$); $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/\varpi_bB$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime ($f\in W_0$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$); the image of $j_q$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under all $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element $b\in B\cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which cuts out $A$ on $k_0$, has the image of $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j_q$ and is such that $p(j_q)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$; and, for each $s'\in W$ with $s'\ne s$, an element $b\in B\cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which cuts out $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfies the analogue of (W2) with $s'$ in place of $s$.
--
--   (D) The Drinfeld clause: for every $(\mathbb F_{q^2}=\mathtt{GaloisField}\,q\,2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ making $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ a domain, and every $\zeta\in\mathtt{Idx}\ q$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ (the fixed field of the subgroup of the Drinfeld function field generated by the action of $C_s$) with: $\#C_s=2\,\mathtt{placeWidthChar}\ q\ M'\ s$; $\ker\rho=(\varpi_b)$; $\rho$ on constants from $A_b$ is reduction to $\kappa$ followed by the structure map; every element of the target is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field comes from the coordinate ring; and equivariance of $\rho$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ in $\mathtt{hSubgroup}\ q$, matching $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ on $B$ with $\mathtt{hFunctionFieldAction}$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   (N) The node clauses: $\#\mathtt{nodes}=q+1$; there is a common subring $B_c\subseteq F_0$, generated by the image of $A\cap k_0$ together with a finite set, which is contained in every $O\in\mathtt{nodes}$ and of which every $O$ is the localisation ($f\in O$ iff $fh=g$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$); the level automorphisms permute $\mathtt{nodes}$, and for each $\zeta$ they act transitively on $\mathtt{nodes}$ in the corresponding sense; distinct nodes are separated by an element which is a non-unit of one and a unit of the other; and a covering clause: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which cuts out $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfies (W2) either contains $B$ or dominates a node, i.e. there is $O\in\mathtt{nodes}$ with $O\subseteq V$ and all non-units of $O$ inside $\mathfrak m_V$. Finally, for each $O\in\mathtt{nodes}$ (the per-node clause, its inner items summarised here): $O\subseteq W_0$, $O$ is local and Noetherian, cuts out $A$ on $k_0$, and each of its elements is congruent to a constant from $A\cap k_0$ modulo non-units; and there exist $E_0\ge1$ with a witness that $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathtt{placeWidthChar}\ q\ M'\ s}v$ for a unit $v$ of $A$ lying in $k_0$, the image of $\pi_0$ in $O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism of the adic completion of $O$ at $\mathfrak m_O$ with the crossing model $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}(\widehat{A_0},\hat\pi_0^{E_0})$, that is $\widehat{A_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$ over the adic completion of $A_0$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ there, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, constants from $A\cap k_0$ correspond to the constants of the model, $c_x\mapsto\gamma_UU$ and $c_y\mapsto\gamma_VV$; $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ while $c_x$, if in $W_0$, is a unit there; the Hasse germ clause that $J-a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and corresponds to a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge1$; the Igusa-branch clause asserting a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, cutting out $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$, possessing an element $t$ whose residue is transcendental in the stated sense, with $c_x\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$, $c_y$ a unit of $W_x$, with the property that modular functions as in (W2) lie in $W_x$ and belong to $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ exactly when their $R_0$-residue vanishes, and lie in $O$ with the expected non-unit congruence when their $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and such that every other node contains a function not lying in $W_x$; and a chart clause asserting a subring $B_x\subseteq B\cap O$ whose elements are regular wherever $j_q$ is, of which $O$ is the localisation and $F_0$ the fraction field, generated by the image of $A\cap k_0$ together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ which lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ of the kind described in (B) which fails to contain all of $O$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every field $\mathit{FSS}$ with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ to $\mathit{FSS}$ (a valuation subring with surjective residue map onto $\mathit{FSS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, cutting out $A$ on constants, inducing $A\to\kappa$ there, and with the scaling property) such that $R.\mathrm{integers}$ meets $F_0$ exactly in $W_0$, there is a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathit{FSS}$ over $\kappa$ with $\#N=q+1$, together with: fields $\mathit{FIx}\,x$ with $\kappa$-algebra structures, regular prolongations $Rx\,x$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ to $\mathit{FIx}\,x$ and places $bx\,x$ of $\mathit{FIx}\,x$ over $\kappa$, indexed by the places $x$ of $\mathit{FSS}$; subrings $C'_l\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l$; types $Wc_l$ which are complete discrete valuation domains, with elements $\pi_l$; naturals $E_l$ and $E_0$; a function $S$ assigning to each place of $\mathit{FSS}$ a set of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; subrings $\mathcal N\,nd$ and $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$, the latter local and Noetherian; and elements $c_x\,nd$, $c_y\,nd$, $c_u\,nd$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$; all satisfying the following.
--
--   First, $C'_n$ is exactly $A\cap K_n$: $c\in C'_n$ iff $c\in A$ and $c$ lies in the image of $K_n$. For $d\in C'_l$ the residue of $d$ in $\kappa$ vanishes iff $d\in\varpi'_lC'_l$; $C'_{n_0}\le C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{n_0}\ne0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $E_l\ge1$. Every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with trivial tame character fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$. There are $w\ge1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}=v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$ in $A$.
--
--   Next, for each $nd\in N$: there is $O\in\mathtt{nodes}$ such that $O$ maps into $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,n_0$, non-units of $O$ going to non-units of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,n_0$; $S\,nd$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which contain $O$ and at which every non-unit $f$ of $O$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in\mathfrak m_A$; the $R$-residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of $nd$, those of non-units of $O$ lying in its maximal ideal; and $nd$ is the unique place of $\mathit{FSS}$ with these last two properties. Moreover $bx\,nd$, $nd$ and every $P\in S\,nd$ are rational; $\mathcal N\,nd$ is exactly the intersection of $(Rx\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$, $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and the valuation subrings of the places in $S\,nd$; for $f\in\mathcal N\,nd$ and $P\in S\,nd$ one has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$; $c_x\,nd\cdot c_y\,nd=(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}\,c_u\,nd$; the $(Rx\,nd)$-residue of $c_x\,nd$ is $0$, the $nd$-order of the $R$-residue of $c_x\,nd$ is $1$, the $R$-residue of $c_y\,nd$ is $0$, and the $(bx\,nd)$-order of the $(Rx\,nd)$-residue of $c_y\,nd$ is $1$ (each under the corresponding integrality hypothesis). For every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character, the semilinear automorphism $g=\mathtt{arithmeticGalois}$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ attached to $\tau$ preserves $S\,nd$ ($P\in S\,nd$ iff $g\cdot P\in S\,nd$) and fixes $c_x\,nd$ and $c_y\,nd$. Every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ is a ratio of elements of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ for some layer $l$ with nonzero denominator, and becomes, after multiplication by a nonzero element of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,n_0$, an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,n_0$.
--
--   For each layer $l$ and each $nd\in N$: $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,n_0\le\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l\le\mathcal N\,nd$; $S\,nd$ is also characterised by $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$, namely as the set of places containing $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ at which every non-unit has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ in $\mathfrak m_A$; $C'_l$ maps into $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$; every element of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ is congruent to a constant from $C'_l$ modulo non-units; families of elements of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ with $C'_l$-linearly independent $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients summing to zero vanish; there is a subring $B_x$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ inside $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ containing $c_x\,nd$, $c_y\,nd$, $c_u\,nd$, of which $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ is the localisation, and which is generated by the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x\,nd$ and $c_y\,nd$ lie in $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ and $c_u\,nd$ is a unit there; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $Wc_l$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ at its maximal ideal and an isomorphism of that completion with the crossing model $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}(Wc_l,\pi_l^{E_l})=Wc_l[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_l^{E_l})$ such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\sigma$ followed by the isomorphism sends $o$ to $\mathtt{const}\,o$, the Hasse germ $J-a_0$ lies in $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ and corresponds to a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge1$, every constant from $C'_l$ is in the image of $\sigma$, and the two order-matching clauses hold: if the $(Rx\,nd)$-residue of $f\in\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ is nonzero of $bx\,nd$-order $n$, then the image of $f$ differs from a unit times $V^n$ by an element of the ideal generated by $\mathtt{const}\,\pi_l$ and $U$; and if the $R$-residue of $f$ is nonzero of $nd$-order $n$, then the image of $f$ differs from a unit times $U^n$ by an element of the ideal generated by $\mathtt{const}\,\pi_l$ and $V$.
--
--   Further, distinct members of $N$ have disjoint $S$-sets: if $P\in S\,nd$ and $P\in S\,nd'$ with $nd,nd'\in N$ then $nd=nd'$. For $nd\in N$ and $P\in S\,nd$, and for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ regular wherever $j_q$ is and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f-a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$. For each $\zeta'\in\mathtt{Idx}\ q$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on the places of $\mathit{FSS}$ such that for $nd\in N$: $\tau_N\,nd\in N$, $(\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,\zeta'\,\gamma)\cdot P\in S\,nd$ iff $P\in S(\tau_N\,nd)$, and the comap of $(Rx\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$ along that automorphism is $(Rx(\tau_N\,nd)).\mathrm{integers}$. For every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ generated by the $\mathtt{levelAutBar}\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every $nd\in N$: the induced residual automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ carries $nd$ into $N$ and $\mathtt{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(S\,nd)=S(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot nd)$. For $nd\in N$, $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ maps into $(Rx\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$, and there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M'$ to $\mathit{FIx}\,nd$ compatible with the residues (the $(Rx\,nd)$-residue of the image of $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ is $j$ of its $R_0$-residue) and such that $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ iff $j(g)$ lies in that of $bx\,nd$. Lastly, for distinct $x,x'\in N$ there is an element $g$ lying in $\mathcal N_0\,x\,n_0$ and in $\mathcal N_0\,x'\,n_0$ which is an associate of $c_x\,x$ in $\mathcal N_0\,x\,n_0$ and a unit of $\mathcal N_0\,x'\,n_0$.
--
--   This is the per-node core of the layered description of the semistable fibre of the full-level modular curve $X_H(q^2M')$, with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, above a supersingular point $s$ of the characteristic-$q$ fibre: it converts a node-by-node local model over the small constant field $k_0$ (crossing presentations $UV=\pi_0^{E_0}$, Hasse germ of $j(\mathsf q^{q})-a_0$ along one branch, Igusa-branch separation) into the corresponding data over the residual prolongation $R$, with $q+1$ nodal places, their residue discs, layerwise crossing models and equivariance for the level automorphisms and for tame inertia. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep).
